{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up","id":1333093,"title":"Third Edition Makarios write-up","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-29T06:17:13-07:00","id":1333093,"title":"Third Edition Makarios write-up","content":"Makarios has always been one of my favourite demons, so now that he's gotten an entry for Third Edition I might as well get a ball rolling on discussing him.<br /> <br /> My feelings are honestly mixed. I do think the Charms are good, with that one in which he's empowered to see through attempts to misrepresent value standing out, but the lack of something related to his crafting feels like an omission. I like how the Merit clarifies the premises around how his sigil actually gets applied and what can happen to it thereafter; it seems to me that the effect is a bit milder, but I can see value in the idea of making bearing the sigil a somewhat more liveable condition for the sake of broadening his customer base.<br /> <br /> Buuutttt\u2026 his character write-up is disappointingly workmanlike. It doesn't really have much personality, doesn't convey the surreal wonder that is supposed to be part and parcel with engaging with him. I don't get why it doesn't have the idea that the dreams themselves are what he fashions his wares from, and I feel as though that removes a key aspect of the cycle that drives him. When the idea is that Makarios is driven to acquire dreams to turn into things that he sells in exchange for more dreams, it gives me the impression that the trade itself is the point, and dreams just happen to be the central commodity because he's a demon and that's his uncanny take on the subject. Looking again, it doesn't even specifically have the idea that they don't dream because Makarios takes them, it just... stops. Without that part, it makes it feel as though depriving people of dreams is the point, and the commerce is just a means towards that end.<br /> <br /> And I've got to say, I just straight up hate that artwork of him. I could get over the hairstyle, the clothes, the build even though they're quite unlike the look of him that I'm used to, but it makes him look unambiguously sinister, and I find that to be quite contrary to the point of Makarios. The impression I've always gotten from Makarios is that he's genuinely amiable and an honest trader who just happens to deal in something kind of terrible, and hence he's supposed to have a look of charm and trustworthiness, something that puts people at ease. This guy looks like he's definitely out to screw you over, and even if that's not what the write-up portends and even if he's still socially advantaged in a manner that could translate into being able to get people to look past his appearance, I find it to be a case of art not effectively conveying premise, and I take issue with it. I also definitely think that there are going to be new people for whom this will be their introduction to Makarios where the picture will make a certain stronger impression than a few lines in the short write-up (not least because, again, it's not very flavourful) and will come away with the standard duplicitous demon bargainer archetype.<br /> <br /> I'm in no way objective about this, and I can even recognise that this is grating against elements of the prior depictions that made a stronger impression on me that may be largely irrelevant to others. But it touches on something that I had a distinct investment in, and I wanted to share the feelings thus provoked.<br /> <br /> (Also, why is he under Hundred Devils Night Parade? I thought that was supposed to be for animals and monsters, not characters with motives and personalities.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T06:43:24-07:00","id":1333095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up#post1333093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, why is he under Hundred Devils Night Parade? I thought that was supposed to be for animals and monsters, not characters with motives and personalities.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is one of those questions which answers themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T06:55:05-07:00","id":1333097,"title":"","content":"I think all the demons are in Hundred Devils","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T07:02:19-07:00","id":1333098,"title":"","content":"It might also be QCs instead of Full Write Ups?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T07:10:36-07:00","id":1333099,"title":"","content":"I wasn't around for 2E so I can't really compare him, but I agree that his whole marking people thing suddenly makes a lot more sense if he's gaining something tangible from it, rather than just doing it out of blue-and-orange morality.<br /> <br /> I do like his artwork. Although the evil grin makes it misleading, I can see that character coming off as a charming trader of wonders when he's not literally grinning at you like a demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-29-2019, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T07:44:05-07:00","id":1333100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up#post1333093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I've got to say, I just straight up hate that artwork of him. I could get over the hairstyle, the clothes, the build even though they're quite unlike the look of him that I'm used to, but it makes him look unambiguously sinister, and I find that to be quite contrary to the point of Makarios. The impression I've always gotten from Makarios is that he's genuinely amiable and an honest trader who just happens to deal in something kind of terrible, and hence he's supposed to have a look of charm and trustworthiness, something that puts people at ease. This guy looks like he's definitely out to screw you over, and even if that's not what the write-up portends and even if he's still socially advantaged in a manner that could translate into being able to get people to look past his appearance, I find it to be a case of art not effectively conveying premise, and I take issue with it. I also definitely think that there are going to be new people for whom this will be their introduction to Makarios where the picture will make a certain stronger impression than a few lines in the short write-up (not least because, again, it's not very flavourful) and will come away with the standard duplicitous demon bargainer archetype.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, that Hundred Devils artwork just does not do it for me, he goes from a friendly-looking man in Ex2 to a creepy punk kid with black claw, pointy ears and punk hair.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/736x/8d/c4/2c/8dc42c06668bdf82102ee6baf94de02c.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> There is no way I'm gonna do any business to someone looking like the guy below for sure.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/287087.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T08:00:34-07:00","id":1333105,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the art, though I agree he seems more an Adversary of the Righteous than a Hundred Devil. My issue with his charm set isn't so much his lack of craft charms, but charms like Waking Dream Affliction and Tarnished Trinket Glint seem to lean more into conning that honest trader.<br /> <br /> My biggest issue? How do you visit him. Or have him visit you. A mean a sorceror could summon him and just send him round someones house, but that hardly seems thematic. He could use Gates of the Dreaming Market, but that requires him to know were the sleeping individual is - which again would presumably require a sorceror to tell him. He could use Sigil-Seeking to make a sense-roll to locate the nearest sigil bearer, but he's in the dreamrealm and the dreamer is in creation - I'm not sure you're entitled to makes sense rolls across metaphysical planes.<br /> <br /> I'll be the first to admit I'm possibly just being dumb here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23614-zardoz","name":"Zardoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23614_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T08:16:03-07:00","id":1333106,"title":"","content":"I assume the point is that when you want to trade with Makarios, you catch a mortal, mark them and then sell him the location.<br /> <br /> As to why he's in Hundred Devils, I assume it's because he's a Devil. There are intelligent behemoths, elements, ghosts and demons in there.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's a Raksha and I think a ghost in Adversaries, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-29-2019, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T08:31:26-07:00","id":1333107,"title":"","content":"More broadly; I don't really have any strong feelings about Makarios. He never caught my interest in 2nd ed, so I'm not hugely bothered if he is different in 3rd. But I can see Isator's point about dreams and surreal wonder. The charms and buying and finding sigils just seems to be missing something to make it click together. (The individual charms seem fine)<br /> <br /> One thing I will say is I'm glad they're doing more 2nd ed demons in the bestiary; I like the various monsters, but honestly haven't found them very useful. What I've found useful are spirits, behemoths, animals that Lunars can turn into, and Exalted NPCs (for example, I used the stats of the Ragara Satrap as a DB the PCs fought recently). But the spirits aren't powerful enough to be a challenge to PCs, they're more for them (or their enemies) to summon.<br /> <br /> The second-circle demons in the Core are fine, but I'm kind of bored with them. The PCs have hung out with Mara loads, fought Octavian, seen Alveua around a lot, etc. And Makarios is quite different.<br /> <br /> So more is good. I hope to see Hundred Devils do even more; perhaps some new or at least less-used (ie from CoCD: Malfeas) ones. <br /> But what I'm really keen on seeing is the Third-Circle Eric wrote!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-29-2019, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T09:18:03-07:00","id":1333109,"title":"","content":"I like how he\u2019s completely Eclipse-keyworded except for the worse Irresistible Salesman Spirit. And we\u2019re about to reach Essence 3 in the game that I\u2019m playing an Eclipse merchant...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T09:31:14-07:00","id":1333111,"title":"","content":"I think he may have more Eclipse keywords than any other spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T09:41:04-07:00","id":1333112,"title":"","content":"I think I asked before about what kinds of characters go under which labels and got an answer that would seem to put Second Circle Demons under Adversaries. But I suppose it's a relatively minor point.<br /> <br /> With a few hours to cool down, I do regret some of my harsher weird choices, although I don't feel any differently about the art work.<br /> <br /> I don't know; I feel as though something about this write-up just doesn't pop. I do still think the Charms are good, but I feel as though something like that needs a strong sense of character. I wouldn't even blame it on the format, since Adeimantus didn't have this issue. Maybe it's just down to one that fell a bit below the mark.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not terrible or anything, I just feel it doesn't quite convey what made the character feel so distinct and interesting.<br /> <br /> But I also think I might not be giving the whole thing fair shakes, just because I first saw it on Facebook, and having that picture attached to the name made an unfortunate first impression.<br /> <br /> Sure, all the information and artwork I like about the character still exists, and isn't really incompatible with these stats. But part of my feeling is that we have an opportunity to introduce new people to what is varied and interesting about these demons (the corebook ones are great, but they're more overtly antagonistic across the board), and it feels like that's been missed here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T11:18:06-07:00","id":1333131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333112#post1333112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, all the information and artwork I like about the character still exists, and isn't really incompatible with these stats. But part of my feeling is that we have an opportunity to introduce new people to what is varied and interesting about these demons (the corebook ones are great, but they're more overtly antagonistic across the board), and it feels like that's been missed here.</div> </div> </div> </div>To play Devil's Antagonist for a moment:<br /> <br /> That seems intentional. Demons have not been portrayed in a sympathetic light this edition. From the personalities showcased in the Corebook, to summoning, to dev commentary about slavery -- demons and their Yozi mistresses are no longer recognised as the former masters of the world but are instead &quot;monsters&quot;, &quot;baleful spirits&quot;, and &quot;dread fiends&quot;.<br /> <br /> The transformation of a kindly craftsman and merchant into a grinning <i>demon</i> looks to me to be a deliberate design choice.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is just my inference. But if any character was going to be used to show that demons are otherworldly but essentially <i>people</i> then it'd be Makarios.<br /> <br /> 3E has done away with a lot of moral complexity and challenging issues. It's still a rich setting, and (I guess) you don't want to be too edgy or inaccessible. And if you're going to vilipend The Realm, you can't exactly lionize demons. If you're going to make mortals matter and have Creation as the setting, you don't want the PCs rushing to dream worlds to cavort with demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T11:25:41-07:00","id":1333134,"title":"","content":"Possibly it\u2019s a word count issue? Because the bits describing him and how he operates seem kinda short, especially as compared to many of the other entries. Maybe cutting or condensing one of his charms would allow for going more in depth into why he does things?<br /> <br /> Alternately, maybe \u201cusing dreams as construction material\u201d is a Raksha thing that they don\u2019t want to explicitly give him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T12:01:21-07:00","id":1333140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333131#post1333131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To play Devil's Antagonist for a moment:<br /> <br /> That seems intentional. Demons have not been portrayed in a sympathetic light this edition. From the personalities showcased in the Corebook, to summoning, to dev commentary about slavery -- demons and their Yozi mistresses are no longer recognised as the former masters of the world but are instead &quot;monsters&quot;, &quot;baleful spirits&quot;, and &quot;dread fiends&quot;.<br /> <br /> The transformation of a kindly craftsman and merchant into a grinning <i>demon</i> looks to me to be a deliberate design choice.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is just my inference. But if any character was going to be used to show that demons are otherworldly but essentially <i>people</i> then it'd be Makarios.<br /> <br /> 3E has done away with a lot of moral complexity and challenging issues. It's still a rich setting, and (I guess) you don't want to be too edgy or inaccessible. And if you're going to vilipend The Realm, you can't exactly lionize demons. If you're going to make mortals matter and have Creation as the setting, you don't want the PCs rushing to dream worlds to cavort with demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>(First, I get that you're playing Devil's Advocate here.)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That seems intentional. Demons have not been portrayed in a sympathetic light this edition. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure there's any big difference. They said they wanted to get away from &quot;the Ebon Dragon is eeeeevil&quot; and &quot;Malfeas hates everything and everyone, smash, smash, smash!&quot;<br /> The demons shown in the Core (and since) seem, well, about the same as before actually. (Honestly I really wish they'd done all new demons; but they didn't, it's all stuff we've seen before except the Fulope, and the personalities of the demons seem just the same as they were in 2nd ed).<br /> <br /> Sure, they're not shown in a sympathetic light (nor, IMO, should they necessarily be), but they're also not shown as DnD-esque demons, which that art looks a little like. (I didn't recognise Makarios at first, tbh, he looks so different. I don't hate it. I don't love it.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The transformation of a kindly craftsman and merchant into a grinning <i>demon</i> looks to me to be a deliberate design choice. </div> </div> </div>I never got the impression he was kindly. Just that he looked kindly, which seemed to me to be, well, part of his manipulation of mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3E has done away with a lot of moral complexity and challenging issues. </div> </div> </div>Has it? It seems to me the main change is that the focus is less on giant clashes of the Good Incarnae and Evil Demon-Lords and more on nations, which are much more morally complex than this apparently-morally-perfect Unconquered Sun (I disliked his portrayal so much I just killed him off in my game).<br /> <br /> Well, that and less magitech, but I don't see that as really being very morally complex.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, Hatewheel was rather keen on &quot;Solars are the good guys, Dragonblood the bad&quot;, but he hasn't been running Ex3 for literally years, he and Holden only wrote one book of the 4+2 segmented bestiaries that have been done, and the 2nd ed Core looked like Solars were the good guys anyway (there were some nice digs, but they were subtle, not overt) so that the 3rd ed book didn't seem like any kind of departure. It mostly came out in his dev comments rather than the book. And he wrote the amazing heroic perfect Ignis Divine for 2nd ed anyway, IIRC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you're going to vilipend The Realm, you can't exactly lionize demons. </div> </div> </div>I assume you mean vilify.<br /> <br /> But you don't exactly need to lionise them to not say &quot;all demons are evil, they love evil and wear big black cloaks and have horns&quot;.<br /> <br /> Saying this, I don't actually get the impression from this release that Makarios is any more villainous than he ever was.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I may be reading too much into what you're saying here.<br /> <br /> But Isator said the demons in the Core are more antagonistic, not that they're more evil than Makarios.<br /> <br /> And I can see the point that Octavian, whether he's more &quot;evil&quot; than Makarios, is someone you're going to either enslave or punch. You're not really going to be going to dinner to discuss business dealings with him. So I can see the point about wanting more... well, not &quot;nice&quot; demons, but ones the players can work with.<br /> <br /> But saying this, I have to disagree with Isator too; I don't think Sigereth or Alveua are really that antagonistic, tbh. Sigereth plays games (scrupulously fairly) and lets you bet stuff. Alveua makes stuff, loves insects, and turns willing souls into items. But if you run into her in a teahouse, you're not immediately going to start a kung-fu fight with her, the way you would with Octavian.<br /> <br /> Mara... is a bit more complex. She may feed on your soul. She may set you up in a doomed relationship. I suppose that's antagonistic, though not the way Octavian is.<br /> <br /> Actually, in our game Mara has made friends with one of our PCs and converted to the Cult of the Illuminated. Now she's essentially the Cult's main sorcerer (there is a sorcerer PC, but they don't get on with the Cult).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On a different topic, has anyone else noticed that of the 5 published Second Circles, 3 are from the Ebon Dragon? And the Third-Circle they said they've written (but it's waiting to be published) is also of the Ebon Dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-29-2019, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T13:35:12-07:00","id":1333160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333107#post1333107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More broadly; I don't really have any strong feelings about Makarios. He never caught my interest in 2nd ed, so I'm not hugely bothered if he is different in 3rd. But I can see Isator's point about dreams and surreal wonder. The charms and buying and finding sigils just seems to be missing something to make it click together. (The individual charms seem fine)<br /> <br /> <b>One thing I will say is I'm glad they're doing more 2nd ed demons in the bestiary</b>; I like the various monsters, but honestly haven't found them very useful. What I've found useful are spirits, behemoths, animals that Lunars can turn into, and Exalted NPCs (for example, I used the stats of the Ragara Satrap as a DB the PCs fought recently). But the spirits aren't powerful enough to be a challenge to PCs, they're more for them (or their enemies) to summon.<br /> <br /> The second-circle demons in the Core are fine, but I'm kind of bored with them. The PCs have hung out with Mara loads, fought Octavian, seen Alveua around a lot, etc. And Makarios is quite different.<br /> <br /> So more is good. I hope to see Hundred Devils do even more; perhaps some new or at least less-used (ie from CoCD: Malfeas) ones.<br /> But what I'm really keen on seeing is the Third-Circle Eric wrote!</div> </div> </div> </div>?<br /> <br /> Makarios was introduced all the way back in Games of Divinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T14:15:25-07:00","id":1333166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333131#post1333131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems intentional. Demons have not been portrayed in a sympathetic light this edition. From the personalities showcased in the Corebook, to summoning, to dev commentary about slavery -- demons and their Yozi mistresses are no longer recognised as the former masters of the world but are instead &amp;quot;monsters&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;baleful spirits&amp;quot;, and &amp;quot;dread fiends&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see it, and would find it to be a misstep if that was the case.<br /> <br /> I find that they can still be dead fiends while still having a diverse range of personalities. I'm still all for Makarios dealing almost solely in dreams in a manner that causes severe neurological harm. Just that he's basically friendly about it, and that for him it's all about the commerce.<br /> <br /> I don't think their status as former matters of the world enters into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3E has done away with a lot of moral complexity and challenging issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Lunar Dominions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you're going to vilipend The Realm, you can't exactly lionize demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting of Exalted is one in which Hell has basically no association with human evil.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't want to lionised Makarios; it's still basically about him trading in souls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to make mortals matter and have Creation as the setting, you don't want the PCs rushing to dream worlds to cavort with demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure you do; demons are an excellent source of magical weapons and the like that are very useful for evening odds or coming at enemy good or Exalted sideways.<br /> <br /> Makarios' best wares should not come cheap. You want that deadly automaton soldier, that's going to cost you the dreams of a couple thousand for about a year. That's enough to keep these things from flooding the setting.<br /> <br /> The agency still lies with the mortal princes because all Makarios wants it of it is to get paid, and maybe have some return business. What you do with your purchase is entirely in you.<br /> <br /> Lunar Dominions are good for presenting that principle as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333134#post1333134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly it\u2019s a word count issue? Because the bits describing him and how he operates seem kinda short, especially as compared to many of the other entries. Maybe cutting or condensing one of his charms would allow for going more in depth into why he does things?<br /> <br /> Alternately, maybe \u201cusing dreams as construction material\u201d is a Raksha thing that they don\u2019t want to explicitly give him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Word count I can see. I wouldn't like it, but I could accept it, albeit with reservations. If writing mechanics means that there's little space to establish personality or a surrounding tone, that's a problem; it was a real weight on the necks of several First Age Exalted back when they needed those really stupidly written gigantic Charm lists.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't accept differentiating from Fair Folk. There should be enough to distinguish them to keep that kind of approach from being proprietary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333140#post1333140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I can see the point that Octavian, whether he's more &amp;quot;evil&amp;quot; than Makarios, is someone you're going to either enslave or punch. You're not really going to be going to dinner to discuss business dealings with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not with that attitude you're not. Guy has Intimacies, he can be socially influenced. Offer him something that will expand his empire. Appeal to his desire to test his strength against the world. Maybe some food that doesn't taste like his ass.<br /> <br /> When I say he's more antagonistic, I'm thinking about how his aspirations on the whole are focused on conquest and combat. On an individual basis, that can still be engaged with in a number of ways, albeit probably ones that end with somebody bleeding.<br /> <br /> Somebody is likely to suffer out of engaging with Makarios as well, but that's not the point for him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But saying this, I have to disagree with Isator too; I don't think Sigereth or Alveua are really that antagonistic, tbh. Sigereth plays games (scrupulously fairly) and lets you bet stuff. Alveua makes stuff, loves insects, and turns willing souls into items. But if you run into her in a teahouse, you're not immediately going to start a kung-fu fight with her, the way you would with Octavian.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I had forgotten Alveua was in there. That said, I've always seen her as a bit... heartless. That whole attitude of reshaping gods and mortals into shapes that are obedient, and equating this with happiness.<br /> <br /> I could make an argument about Sigereth, but right now it feels a little bit obtuse. The main thing I'll say is that Makarios is more transactional; you pay a fair price (in a horror story currency) and get something in exchange. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mara... is a bit more complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Her defining principle is that she takes pleasure in death and suffering.<br /> <br /> There are other things against her, but I feel as though those are kind of gilding the lily when I start at the point of her defining principle bring taking pleasure in death and suffering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different topic, has anyone else noticed that of the 5 published Second Circles, 3 are from the Ebon Dragon? And the Third-Circle they said they've written (but it's waiting to be published) is also of the Ebon Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that has anything to do with the Ebon Dragon, just those three happen to be popular demons.<br /> <br /> Mara was chosen by a backer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T15:28:07-07:00","id":1333170,"title":"","content":"With Makarios' appearance I always viewed him as a shapeshifter when he's doing the dream thing, granted not in a way that allows him to be an imposter just that when its a dream he goes that extra step in appearing as someone his potential clients would deal with. IE if the glowing green eyes would freak people out then he'd have more normal human eyes for the dream sale. The appearance they gave I interpreted as a default form that he tends to take when a summoner has him materialized in Creation as opposed to just working the dream angle.<br /> <br /> That said I like most of the write-up I will however agree that it is a bit of a shame to leave out the bit on how he can make things from the dreams given to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T17:26:18-07:00","id":1333190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333170#post1333170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if the glowing green eyes</div> </div> </div> </div>Some very dull prisms going around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T18:36:08-07:00","id":1333199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333134#post1333134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly it\u2019s a word count issue? Because the bits describing him and how he operates seem kinda short, especially as compared to many of the other entries. Maybe cutting or condensing one of his charms would allow for going more in depth into why he does things?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my impression as well. Compared to Games of Divinity, this write-up seems to focus more on Makarios spreading his sigil specifically rather than his merchant empire in general. There's <i>a lot</i> you can do with that (dreams as a metaphor for desires, choosing to prey on human greed over any other suitable means, the boundary between the real and unreal, etc.) but the text doesn't delve into the implications, so it kind of falls flat. <br /> <br /> Still really happy with it though. Makarios is tied with Sigereth as my favourite demon and this is the only issue of Hundred Devils Night Parade I've bought so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T00:27:19-07:00","id":1333227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333160#post1333160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ?<br /> <br /> Makarios was introduced all the way back in Games of Divinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did the rest of the paragraph not make that clear? I meant that they're doing 3rd edition stats for more 2nd circle demons.<br /> <br /> I suppose I can write my own stats for previously-introduced demons (I did for Florivet and Iyutha) but I would rather have official ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-30-2019, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T02:47:00-07:00","id":1333233,"title":"","content":"The writeup doesn\u2019t bother me overmuch, but that art, I half-expect Makarios to ask if I \u201c<i>want to see something strange and mystical</i>.\u201d<br /> <br /> He\u2019s so overtly sinister that it feels like I can\u2019t show it to my players without them assuming that he\u2019s <i>supposed</i> to be obviously untrustworthy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\"><b>NO!! Get out of here with that watch! Lay off the poor beavers, will ya? Sheesh!!</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-30-2019, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T04:07:23-07:00","id":1333235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333227#post1333227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did the rest of the paragraph not make that clear?</div> </div> </div> </div>This paragraph?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>I like the various monsters, but honestly haven't found them very useful. What I've found useful are spirits, behemoths, animals that Lunars can turn into, and Exalted NPCs (for example, I used the stats of the Ragara Satrap as a DB the PCs fought recently). But the spirits aren't powerful enough to be a challenge to PCs, they're more for them (or their enemies) to summon.</i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant that they're doing 3rd edition stats for more 2nd circle demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but you said Second <u>Ed</u> demons up there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 08-30-2019, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T04:41:32-07:00","id":1333236,"title":"","content":"For all that talk about octavian having intimacies, you are awfully unwilling to see <i>people that are willing to sell mortal souls</i> would sit down and talk to the guy in a dream.<br /> <br /> It's just a punkier appearance. There are plenty lunars and dynasts I'd hesitate longer to sit down and talk.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T05:03:13-07:00","id":1333237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333235#post1333235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This paragraph?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not really...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, but you said Second <u>Ed</u> demons up there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I misunderstood Saur Ops Specialist's point. I thought they meant that Makarios isn't new.<br /> <br /> Actually, I did mean to write 2nd circle, but it's not important; 1st circles would also be useful, though less so (there's, what, 4 published 1st circle and 5 published 2nd circle? And 0 published 3rd circles. That's the one I would most like to see).<br /> <br /> I'm glad they're releasing 3rd edition rules for 2nd ed* demons, as I find them useful, and I hope for more, and maybe even entirely new ones.<br /> <br /> *Whether they are also 1st ed demons isn't very important to me. I can't think of any 1st ed demons that are not also 2nd ed demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-30-2019, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T07:19:00-07:00","id":1333244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333236#post1333236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all that talk about octavian having intimacies, you are awfully unwilling to see <i>people that are willing to sell mortal souls</i> would sit down and talk to the guy in a dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>That alone conveys a bias that I'm distressed to be associated with the demon. When Makarios has a persona and assistance that conveys the impression that he's trustworthy and sincere, it more readily cultivates narratives in which people will opt to pay in their <i>own</i> dreams.<br /> <br /> The elements together mean that I've always liked the idea that in transactions with Makarios, the human is the one who's going to be the asshole; the one who'll opt to make another pay on their behalf, or even try to cheat out of paying at all. Makarios is ever forthright.<br /> <br /> They're facets that broaden the range of interactions with him, the kinds of people that might feel comfortable engaging with him.<br /> <br /> That and I just like the demons to cover a variety. There's already too much of a bias towards presuming the wicked and the sinister, some effort needs to be exerted to keep focus on the actual interesting Hell that we've got.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you get stuff like people presuming that neomah are definitely going to make evil scary babies, or writing Demon-Blooded as needing to recover Essence in &quot;places of sin&quot;.<br /> <br /> This would be why I would object if it turned out that the intent is that the Exalted aren't even capable of paying in their dreams. You take away the option to sacrifice oneself, it makes actions harming others a bit more forced and less meaningful. Conversely, if they can make the payments but suffer no deleterious effects, them they're just given an easy out from being morally compromised.<br /> <br /> You can engage with Octavian in a variety of ways because there's a social system, but he's still always the asshole. You might be as well, but he definitely is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just a punkier appearance. There are plenty lunars and dynasts I'd hesitate longer to sit down and talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I'm fine with even a fictional human being more than their appearance, but I find that spirits are a bit more archetypal, wear their symbolism on their sleeves, and that it would be especially helpful for conveying this game's novel take on the meaning of the term demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T07:46:17-07:00","id":1333255,"title":"","content":"The 100Devils write-up is so concise that they wouldn't be able to change Makarios if they wanted. It's the exact same guy, only his appearance changed.<br /> <br /> Makarios always was shady. His dealings are shady. He treasures his commercial empire, he tries very hard to spread his dream-stealing, soul-hooking sigils, and the particulars of that were never nice.<br /> He presents himself as an honest trader, and the parts of that that were true before remain true now: He <b>will</b> give you a fair price, and he will demand as much from you.<br /> <br /> The only thing that truly, radically changed from his appearance is that he doesn't look gentle anymore. He still looks rich, and he will still visit you in your dreams to bargain.<br /> And if you look the writeup from 2e, even that didn't change that much. It's still a copper-haired, prism-eyed dream visitor. That lineart uses basically the same clothes.<br /> <br /> And if you look the writeup from 1e, these renditions are <i>gentler</i>. The sigil explicitly maddens, and it focuses more on how good-looking he is.<br /> <br /> 3e Makarios is faithful to all that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T08:22:02-07:00","id":1333260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333255#post1333255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 100Devils write-up is so concise that they wouldn't be able to change Makarios if they wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot parse this sentence. Who is changing what now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makarios always was shady. His dealings are shady. He treasures his commercial empire, he tries very hard to spread his dream-stealing, soul-hooking sigils, and the particulars of that were never nice.<br /> He presents himself as an honest trader, and the parts of that that were true before remain true now: He <b>will</b> give you a fair price, and he will demand as much from you.</div> </div> </div> </div>For previous depictions I agree to a point, but still value the idea of him being very agreeable and that to him, this is all perfectly normal, because it emphasizes what makes the game's take on demons different. People often like to talk up the point that the game's demons aren't evil, just alien, but we need examples for that to come across and soak people's imaginations so that they don't fall back on what is rote.<br /> <br /> Makarios is shady to the extent that all capitalism is somewhat shady, bit I liked the idea of him as primarily a demon capitalist. As I've said, I find the point where his dream payment doesn't go anywhere to make it feel as though that, rather than the mercantilism, is the point, and I think it shifts the tone of him in a way that makes him more rote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that truly, radically changed from his appearance is that he doesn't look gentle anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>And when creating expectations around something called a demon who is engaging in bargains, that distinction matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T08:52:11-07:00","id":1333262,"title":"","content":"&quot;I cannot parse this sentence. Who is changing what now?&quot;<br /> You are complaining about the 3e Makarios' writing.<br /> It's not doing anything the previous writings of his didn't, except for a couple elements of his appearance. There isn't word count to change him even if that was the intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333260#post1333260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For previous depictions I agree to a point, but still value the idea of him being very agreeable and that to him, this is all perfectly normal, because it emphasizes what makes the game's take on demons different. People often like to talk up the point that the game's demons aren't evil, just alien, but we need examples for that to come across and soak people's imaginations so that they don't fall back on what is rote.<br /> <br /> Makarios is shady to the extent that all capitalism is somewhat shady, bit I liked the idea of him as primarily a demon capitalist. As I've said, I find the point where his dream payment doesn't go anywhere to make it feel as though that, rather than the mercantilism, is the point, and I think it shifts the tone of him in a way that makes him more rote.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> And when creating expectations around something called a demon who is engaging in bargains, that distinction matters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> And this is why I think you read too much into a single lineart of a single edition. He never looked deceptively kind. A bland smile and short hair became a punk haircut and a grin.<br /> If anything, it's that lineart that did him a little bit of a disservice.<br /> <br /> That particular clash you are reporting, it seems, comes far more from your story using the demon than the demon's writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 08-30-2019, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T09:40:57-07:00","id":1333271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333262#post1333262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I cannot parse this sentence. Who is changing what now?&quot;<br /> You are complaining about the 3e Makarios' writing.<br /> It's not doing anything the previous writings of his didn't, except for a couple elements of his appearance. There isn't word count to change him even if that was the intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Low word count doesn't rule out the ability to change something drastically. 2e massively changed the Ebon Dragon with just a capsule description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And this is why I think you read too much into a single lineart of a single edition. He never looked deceptively kind. A bland smile and short hair became a punk haircut and a grin.<br /> If anything, it's that lineart that did him a little bit of a disservice.<br /> <br /> That particular clash you are reporting, it seems, comes far more from your story using the demon than the demon's writeup. </div> </div> </div>Then ignore the lineart from 2e and dig back to the description in GoD, which describes &quot;a charming lad&quot;, not mentioning anything like a sneer or leering grin - it would have been in the original text there if that was the intent, because there was no fat in that chapter. The deceptive thing about Makarios's appearance is that he has rainbow yes and his hair is copper wire, and that people that see it tend to ignore that part, which is little different from any other sign of a spirit's nature leaking through. It's in his nature to appeal, but the art looks like Peter Parker after he started acting grimy and weird in Spider Man 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T09:46:18-07:00","id":1333272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333271#post1333271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then ignore the lineart from 2e and dig back to the description in GoD, which describes &quot;a charming lad&quot;, not mentioning anything like a sneer or leering grin - it would have been in the original text there if that was the intent, because there was no fat in that chapter. The deceptive thing about Makarios's appearance is that he has rainbow yes and his hair is copper wire, and that people that see it tend to ignore that part, which is little different from any other sign of a spirit's nature leaking through. It's in his nature to appeal, but the art looks like Peter Parker after he started acting grimy and weird in Spider Man 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>The art also looks like he's well into explaining to that lady she's about to steal some peoples' dreams.<br /> I find it faithful to his description.<br /> <br /> We can certainly disagree on this..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T10:16:31-07:00","id":1333275,"title":"","content":"The difference between the two images, both being quite clearly different perspectives on the same creature, is also useful to remind us that he can be viewed in different ways by different characters...and different players.<br /> <br /> No one here will do the character a disservice for not using either image. Take his write up and make it your own for your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T19:37:45-07:00","id":1333340,"title":"","content":"I've been waiting for a while to get more Second Circle Demons in the monthlies, and overall I like this. Makario's powers are pretty fun and concise, and while I'm of a mixed mind on the art, it works fine - though it conveys a very different and more straighforwardly suspicious seeming than what I remember of his past presentation. In that sense, I feel the same for some of the Demon art in the core, but I don't think it's in itself inaccurate to his character.<br /> <br /> The dream-crafted wares being de-emphasized and his presentation not going into more detail of how his priorities as a supernatural being run there or his merchantile empire, <i>are</i> a bit of a shame. I think many of the Second Circle Demons in past editions have genuinely interesting or unusual characters, and I'd love it if a bit more wordcount could be found to show that. Another paragraph for Makarios could have introduced some more context for him quite easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-30-2019, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T11:39:26-07:00","id":1333412,"title":"","content":"Is people's problem with the picture that he looks too much like a DnD demon? Because I don't find him particularly threatening or objectively evil-looking, he's not stabbing someone or something; but I can see that his pointed ears and long nails might evoke the look of a DnD demon (or anime demon, actually, they're often shown with pointed ears), which makes people think &quot;oh, he looks evil&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T07:09:30-07:00","id":1333523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333412#post1333412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is people's problem with the picture that he looks too much like a DnD demon? Because I don't find him particularly threatening or objectively evil-looking, he's not stabbing someone or something; but I can see that his pointed ears and long nails might evoke the look of a DnD demon (or anime demon, actually, they're often shown with pointed ears), which makes people think &amp;quot;oh, he looks evil&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more thinking he looks like a stereotypical trickster or fair folk. I liked old markarios. Made him seem like any kind of businessman you can find in a town hall. Just one that deals in artifacts and dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T07:23:32-07:00","id":1333528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333412#post1333412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I don't find him particularly threatening or objectively evil-looking, he's not stabbing someone or something</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Not stabbing someone is the bar you set for a character looking sinister or untrustworthy?<br /> <br /> Do you know what this Makarios looks like to me? He looks like the average Disney villain skipping past even the attempt at dissembling. Those being characters who are able to project a sense of untrustworthiness through things like the shape of their face and how those convey emotions to the audience, which is fairly face-oriented as a result of consisting of human beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see that his pointed ears and long nails might evoke the look of a DnD demon (or anime demon, actually, they're often shown with pointed ears), which makes people think &amp;quot;oh, he looks evil&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you not see how his pointed smile and the crook of his eyebrows is evocative of the look of a person that one should be cautious around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T07:50:48-07:00","id":1333532,"title":"","content":"Not really, no. In my experience people who you should be cautious around are generally really friendly and shake your hand enthusiastically, tell you that you should be happy because the company is going to make loads of money (but not you), are drunk and shouting swear words, speak with an upper-class accent, or are emaciated because they take heroin instead of eating.<br /> <br /> To me, he just looks like he's haggling. Well, actually he looks like he's going &quot;Aha, but!&quot;<br /> He's not wearing black or stroking his evil goatee or whatever.<br /> <br /> I mean, I understand what you're getting at. I understand that Jaffar looks like a villain (a small child once told me I looked like an evil wizard because I had a black beard like Jaffar. Whereas her father's massive beard was white, meaning he was a good wizard). I just don't really get a strong vibe of that from this picture. I can kind of see how you can get it if you look at it in a certain way. But it's not the overwhelming impression to me.<br /> This is probably something quite subjective though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T09:53:29-07:00","id":1333540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333412#post1333412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is people's problem with the picture that he looks too much like a DnD demon? Because I don't find him particularly threatening or objectively evil-looking, he's not stabbing someone or something; but I can see that his pointed ears and long nails might evoke the look of a DnD demon (or anime demon, actually, they're often shown with pointed ears), which makes people think &amp;quot;oh, he looks evil&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, run &quot;how to draw villains&quot; through your favourite search engine.<br /> <br /> I got this: <a href=\"https://drawinghub.com/tut/how-to-draw-villains-26849\" target=\"_blank\">https://drawinghub.com/tut/how-to-draw-villains-26849</a><br /> <br /> Which is basically a step by step guide on how to draw Makarios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T11:37:43-07:00","id":1333571,"title":"","content":"So, it looks like an Eclipse who learned Gates of the Dreaming Market could use it to easily transfer anything they can carry to or from a distant ally?<br /> <br /> I'm sure Makarios himself would never give something away for free (and possibly he might not even accept things for free), but the Charm itself doesn't require that the exchanges be part of an actual bargain.<br /> <br /> As for the art, though, the 3e picture makes me think &quot;trickster imp&quot; and not &quot;merchant of wonders.&quot; Admittedly, Makarios does have elements of both, but I think the latter is a lot more core to his concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T14:03:21-07:00","id":1333595,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I kinda assumed the person we see on the right of the image (the one with their back to the &quot;camera&quot;) is the actual Makarios?<br /> <br /> Because that hair looks more like copper wire to me, and they're wearing the white and green colors associated with Makarios. The person sitting down also has solidly colored glowing eyes instead of the rainbow shimmer Makarios is described with.<br /> <br /> Am I the only one in that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Let us take men and give them the favor of the gods and use them as our champions against the Primordials, that we might overthrow them and play for ourselves the Games of Divinity.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2272-senresk","name":"senresk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T14:30:22-07:00","id":1333605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333571#post1333571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it looks like an Eclipse who learned Gates of the Dreaming Market could use it to easily transfer anything they can carry to or from a distant ally?<br /> <br /> I'm sure Makarios himself would never give something away for free (and possibly he might not even accept things for free), but the Charm itself doesn't require that the exchanges be part of an actual bargain.<br /> <br /> As for the art, though, the 3e picture makes me think &quot;trickster imp&quot; and not &quot;merchant of wonders.&quot; Admittedly, Makarios does have elements of both, but I think the latter is a lot more core to his concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, Makarios in prior editions was incapable of giving anything away for free without bargaining, even if summoned and bound. The summoner had to beat the hell out of him and force him to cough up his wares in order to get something without going through Makarios's business channel, which limited what you could get from him to whatever he had on hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T15:47:50-07:00","id":1333615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333605#post1333605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact, Makarios in prior editions was incapable of giving anything away for free without bargaining, even if summoned and bound. The summoner had to beat the hell out of him and force him to cough up his wares in order to get something without going through Makarios's business channel, which limited what you could get from him to whatever he had on hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like he's got basically the same trait in 3e, too (Demon-Merchant's Prerogative). That's sort of important -- sorcerers with Demon of the Second Circle are powerful enough without being able to whistle up Makarios and force him to hand over everything he's got.<br /> <br /> The poor guy would never manage to turn a profit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T17:32:53-07:00","id":1333623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>senresk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333595#post1333595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I kinda assumed the person we see on the right of the image (the one with their back to the &quot;camera&quot;) is the actual Makarios?<br /> <br /> Because that hair looks more like copper wire to me, and they're wearing the white and green colors associated with Makarios. The person sitting down also has solidly colored glowing eyes instead of the rainbow shimmer Makarios is described with.<br /> <br /> Am I the only one in that?</div> </div> </div> </div>-The rainbow shimmer is depicted by the 2 rainbow-colored vertical lines that run across his eyes. His eyes glow yellow because they're in the middle of the lines and the color yellow appears in the middle of rainbows.<br /> <br /> -He's supplementing his bargain roll by making an illusory castle appear behind him, which wouldn't make sense if he was the one facing the castle.<br /> <br /> -The sigil is floating roughly above where his hand is pointing, and he looks very much like he is explaining how to pay him by marking mortals with said sigil.<br /> <br /> -The white and green character is coded as feminine, whereas Makarios is consistently referred to as he.<br /> <br /> Failing all that, Not showing Makarios' face in his own Hundred Devils picture would be a serious failure of presentation, which I assume Onyx Path is experienced enough to avoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-01-2019, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T17:55:38-07:00","id":1333625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>senresk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333595#post1333595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I kinda assumed the person we see on the right of the image (the one with their back to the &quot;camera&quot;) is the actual Makarios?<br /> <br /> Because that hair looks more like copper wire to me, and they're wearing the white and green colors associated with Makarios. The person sitting down also has solidly colored glowing eyes instead of the rainbow shimmer Makarios is described with.<br /> <br /> Am I the only one in that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rainbow shine is in the glow projecting from the yellow eyes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T06:14:28-07:00","id":1333815,"title":"","content":"[<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333532#post1333532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, no. In my experience people who you should be cautious around are generally really friendly and shake your hand enthusiastically, tell you that you should be happy because the company is going to make loads of money (but not you), are drunk and shouting swear words, speak with an upper-class accent</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some of these can be somewhat difficult to shorthand in a static illustration. Mind, they'd also be a preferable look for the character; at least they'd have a bit more subtlety.<br /> <br /> They'd be more true to life, but they don't really affect the way that this character looks like Mr Burns calling over the prospect of buying a litter of greyhound puppies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, he just looks like he's haggling. Well, actually he looks like he's going &amp;quot;Aha, but!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking like somebody healing is not mutually exclusive with looking like somebody nakedly sinister.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's not wearing black or stroking his evil goatee or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he's only a hair below it, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333571#post1333571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it looks like an Eclipse who learned Gates of the Dreaming Market could use it to easily transfer anything they can carry to or from a distant ally?<br /> <br /> I'm sure Makarios himself would never give something away for free (and possibly he might not even accept things for free), but the Charm itself doesn't require that the exchanges be part of an actual bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, an Eclipse can probably get a large and versatile amount of utility out of learning that power.<br /> <br /> I will give praise to it greatly streamlining the process of Makarios actually delivering the goods. First Edition made it extremely costly in motes and successes, and Second Edition... I'm not quite sure, some combination of spirit Charms seems to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T07:36:58-07:00","id":1333825,"title":"","content":"I think Levi's point is that Makarios looks like a scheming gremlin, while the appearance Mak should be evoking is affable merchant. And one of the big reasons for this is that players are going to come to the table and setting with their own particular bias about &quot;demon merchants&quot; so all that can be done by the game line to play against those assumptions is to the good, and illustrations that don't end up working against what's already a difficult uphill climb.<br /> <br /> The artwork and sparse text aside, I ~do~ really appreciate the number and depth of description we get for Mak's charms. I have a Twilight in my current game that made a deal for the purchase of an object to use in a sorcerous working, and the rules here finally give me some meat to hang on the bones of what the bargain and sigil-marking really means.<br /> <br /> I dunno, it's a nixed bag. On one side it feels lacking if some of the parts that make Makarios unique, on the other hand I appreciate the 'gamability' of his statblock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T11:48:22-07:00","id":1333865,"title":"","content":"Is it possible there's a lack of communication between writers and illustrators? I remember the Storm Serpent illustration was a painfully generic green <i>Lung</i> dragon as opposed to what the actual writeup said (something along the lines of &quot;serpent the color of stormclouds&quot;) and as well as illustrators not being familiar with past illustrations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T11:57:21-07:00","id":1333868,"title":"","content":"He's a young man with prism eyes and similar clothing to before. So I imagine they gave the artist a description. But the artist might have been told &quot;demon merchant who looks like a young man with prism eyes&quot; and assumed he should look, well, demonic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T14:49:52-07:00","id":1333883,"title":"","content":"He's also described as good looking or appealing, and his dream visits haunting and opulent. You pop in my head and sit on an ivory throne before a table made of a single sapphire, the last thing I'll be inclined to trust is a kind smile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-03T20:33:18-07:00","id":1333921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1333093-third-edition-makarios-write-up?p=1333883#post1333883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's also described as good looking or appealing, and his dream visits haunting and opulent. You pop in my head and sit on an ivory throne before a table made of a single sapphire, the last thing I'll be inclined to trust is a kind smile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonetheless, it's his nature to look and act that way. If it doesn't work for everyone, so be it. Plenty of fish in the Great Western Sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}